# pnpm-specific settings do NOT live here any more. pnpm 10+ reads them from
# pnpm-workspace.yaml and silently ignores them in this file - see that file's
# `settings` block, which carries them and the reasoning.
#
# Anything genuinely npm-level (registry, auth) still belongs here. The file is
# kept rather than deleted so the next person looking for `node-linker` finds
# this pointer instead of nothing.
